    <!-- ============ SECTION 1: WORTH IT ============ -->
    <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />
    <h2 id="worth-it" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🤔 Is the Forbidden City Worth Visiting?</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-8">It's well worth a visit — it is a UNESCO World Heritage Site and the world's largest and best-preserved complex of wooden palace architecture. It once served as the residence and center of power for 24 emperors of the Ming and Qing dynasties. Behind the red walls and yellow tiles, and among the tiered palaces, lie 600 years of imperial history — from coronation ceremonies to life in the harem. In every corner, visitors can directly experience the grandeur of ancient Chinese royalty and the architectural ingenuity of the era. For foreign visitors, it is not merely "an old building," but a gateway to understanding Chinese history and culture — as you walk across the plaza of the Hall of Supreme Harmony, you will understand why the Chinese often say that the "Forbidden City" embodies the order and aesthetics of an entire empire.</p>

    <!-- ============ SECTION 2: TICKETS ============ -->
    <hr class="border-gray-200 my-12" />
    <h2 id="tickets" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🎫 How Much Are Forbidden City Tickets? (Official Prices and Booking)</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-8">The Forbidden City is one of the few places in China where the <em>planning</em> is almost as important as the visit itself. Here's everything you need to know, based on the museum's official ticketing rules.</p>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-8">From the Palace Museum's official ticketing policy:</p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-12 not-prose">
